+# Mathematical approaches and decisions
+
+| Approach | Actual new mechanism | Outcome and next obligation |
+|---|---|---|
+| Local ground-density comparison | Compare conditional compact heat kernels | Earlier draft has a useful local ratio; it was not sufficient by itself to multiply rare-event probabilities |
+| Dense magnetic events plus spatial/time chessboard | Disjoint Brownian faces, Schur norm and reflected dissemination | Proposed volume-uniform joint bounds here; shared boundaries and multiplicities checked |
+| Constrained whole-interval path kernels | Excursion forces action or a Brownian escape; even trace powers handle indefinite kernels | Proposed continuous-time event bound; no time regulator introduced |
+| Reversible diffusion compactness | Forward/backward martingales cancel ground drift | Uniform fourth moments and subsequential continuous paths; no uniqueness claim |
+| Temporal oscillations and cubical topology | Independent Brownian edge events and d^2=0 | Closed coarse current with finite components in an explicit small-g range |
+| Response/effective-action comparison | Couple rare currents to the smooth gauge field and physical source | Open; no polymer activity or susceptibility estimate inferred solely from support probabilities |
+
+These are not five refutations of one no-go. No approach is labelled
+exhausted merely because its terminal obligation remains open. The next
+campaign should attack the last row directly, or a scientifically distinct
+native-action obligation if the response route has no concrete mechanism.
