+
+| Input | Role and provenance | Status of the physical bridge |
+|---|---|---|
+| H=-(g^2/2)Delta+g^(-2)sum(1-cos F) on compact link angles | Supplied model, fully restated in the magnetic-event note | Selection from native axioms remains open |
+| Three-dimensional periodic cubic spatial lattice, even L>=4 | Declared theorem domain; zero-temperature then spatial subsequence | Not a proof for arbitrary boundaries or a unique vacuum |
+| 0<g<=1, fixed in L; T>0 fixed | Declared parameters; explicit sufficient examples .01 and .004 | No experimental calibration or sharp transition claim |
+| Compact Feynman-Kac representation, Schur bound, compact positive ground | Established mathematical tools with domains spelled out in the notes | No unlabelled phase premise |
+| Algebraic chessboard estimate | Biskup Theorem5.8, read in primary source; link/path and rectangle hypotheses matched explicitly | Generic quantum site-RP is not assumed |
+| Forward/backward diffusion identity | Smooth finite-volume derivation here; Trutnau primary theorem credited | No limiting SDE or uniform ground drift bound assumed |
+| Principal branch and temporal gauge A_time=0 | Explicit representation conventions, not new dynamics | Full physical electric/4D gauge identification is still open |
+| Integer cochain conservation | Derived here from d^2=0 with orientation conventions | Coarse current is not declared to exhaust every winding sector |
