+approved kinetic primitive are unchanged. No action, coupling, law,
+measure, selected vacuum, matter content, empirical value or unapproved
+primitive is inferred from them in this packet.
+
+Dependency graph: the magnetic-event theorem establishes the model,
+ground energy and reflection/chessboard lemmas; the whole-interval
+theorem reuses those and proves its own kernel bound; the path-limit
+theorem has an independent tightness proof and then transfers the
+whole-interval bounds; the coarse-current theorem adds a temporal
+oscillation bound and integer topology. All four share the same
+unreviewed chessboard/carrier bridge. Its failure would invalidate the
+event and current claims, but not the separately proved reversible
+diffusion moment estimate. Personal finite checks do not confer an
