+# Author claim scope
+
+```yaml
+actual_current_surface_status: conditional-support
+target_claim_type: bounded_theorem
+trace_class: upstream_support
+reachability_to_target: supports
+conditional_surface_status: "Theorems for the explicitly supplied rotor Hamiltonian and specified limits; independent review pending."
+hypothetical_axiom_status: "No new axiom is proposed or assumed."
+admitted_observation_status: "No observed or fitted physical values enter."
+claim_type_reason: "Uniform path-event estimates and a coarse current construction under a declared Hamiltonian and geometry."
+audit_required_before_effective_retained: true
+bare_retained_allowed: false
+```
+
+| Scientific part | Strongest proposed result | Limits |
+|---|---|---|
+| Magnetic sampled events | Joint-event bound uniform in even L | Supplied pure rotor, fixed g and observation spacing |
+| Magnetic excursions | Full-interval supremum bound | Sparse magnetic cover, not a photon theorem |
+| Spatial path limit | Subsequential continuous-path compact Gibbs law with the same bounds | No uniqueness, no free-box identification, no Lorentz limit |
+| Temporal/coarse currents | Joint temporal oscillation bound, exact conserved integer current, exponential component tail | Fixed coarse T, no exhaustive microscopic current or harmonic-sector classification |
+
+All proofs are proposed here and have personal challenge checks. There is
+no independent reviewer, auditor verdict, retained promotion, merge or
+axiom update. The small finite-clock strip tests reflection algebra only;
+it does not inherit the Brownian weak-coupling bounds. The single-rotor
+heat and moment checks are finite-cutoff numerical comparisons and are
+not rigorous infinite-dimensional error enclosures.
