+# Conservative N1-N8 scope check
+
+This packet proposes positive conditional results. Its named downstream
+gaps and explicit countercontrols are recorded here conservatively because
+the N-gate trigger is broad. This is not a formal restricted-audit N-gate
+certificate and no negative retained claim is requested.
+
+**N1. Routes.** The six rows of the approach registry are real approaches
+or open next steps. They are not five failed attempts to prove one claim.
+The two countercontrols are existence constructions in their specified
+finite systems. A five-refutation certificate would be inappropriate and
+is not supplied. The formal schema remains pending if later registration
+classifies a claim as requiring it.
+
+**N2. Independence.** Supplying H is one model-selection condition shared
+by all notes. Reflection/chessboard is one shared mathematical dependency.
+Source response, global harmonic sectors and microscopic T->0 current
+identification are distinct future obligations; they are not additional
+hypotheses silently imposed on the event theorems. No count of walls is
+used in a headline.
+
+**N3. Hidden conditions.** The source states compact Haar angles, full
+unprojected finite-temperature trace followed by its neutral ground limit,
+even L>=4, fixed g, fixed T and the principal orientation convention.
+No unique spatial limit, positive-semidefinite constrained excursion
+kernel, finite-clock Brownian behavior or physical photon gap is assumed.
+The standard chessboard theorem has its path/support hypotheses matched.
+
+**N4. Citation matching.** Biskup supports the algebraic chessboard step,
+not a gauge photon result; its generic quantum warning is explicitly
+addressed. Trutnau supports the reversible identity, not thermodynamic
+uniqueness. Previous PR8164 is contextual only and is not an omitted
+scientific dependency. Native-string literature supplies no proof input.
+
+**N5. Resolutions.** Individual circle paths and finite periodic geometry
+are checked; a12-link binary strip tests reflection algebra; single-rotor
+cutoffs test heat/moment constants. Volume-uniform and infinite-volume
+claims are analytic derivations, not numerical sweeps. There is no N5
+execution certificate in a canonical cache; raw author outputs are not
+mislabelled as one.
+
+**N6. Partial closure.** Whole-interval magnetic events improve sampled
+control; temporal oscillation adds a concrete winding-sensitive bound;
+cubical topology then defines a coarse conserved current. These partial
+closures use no new primitive. No sentence asserts that the registry lacks
+a required primitive or that an axiom change is necessary.
+
+**N7. Steelman.** A reviewer can accept the event inequalities yet reject
+their phase relevance until the exact smooth-field/current weight and
+physical electric source are controlled. Sparse support alone does not
+give conditional polymer activities or an effective-action derivative
+bound. The next campaign must derive that bridge, not assume a photon
+because currents are finite. Conversely, those missing steps may well
+be provable; this record offers no no-go against them.
+
+**N8. Cross-cycle comparison.** Earlier PR8164 obtained local density and
+short-time bridge bounds but left repeated composition/winding/phase
+open. This packet supplies a different path-event mechanism and a fixed-T
+coarse current construction. Its local limits are torus subsequences,
+not the earlier unique cofinal free-box angle limit. Mean defect-density
+control in current main is weaker than the claimed joint-event bound,
+but no retained status is transferred from that earlier result.
