+# Next scientific opportunities
+
+1. Determine whether the actual coarse compact kernel admits a controlled
+   positive current/smooth-field decomposition with source derivatives.
+   The new event bounds are relevant input, but do not supply conditional
+   weights. First decisive step: derive the exact coarse kernel/current
+   representation and identify its normalization and sign, before importing
+   a polymer or homogenization theorem. This has direct leverage on the
+   fixed-g photon/response question.
+2. Seek a nonlocal phase corrector for the electric susceptibility. Earlier
+   local sine-loop certificates lose their lower bound at small momentum;
+   sparse compact branch regions may support a different construction.
+   First discriminator: build a periodic corrector with controlled gradient
+   cost, including branch jumps and harmonic sectors. No uniform estimate
+   is currently established.
+3. Review native Hamiltonian selection and the record-to-action gap against
+   latest main. The supplied-H results cannot establish the TOE without this
+   bridge. Prefer a new quantified mechanism or full-premise counterexample
+   to repeating known restricted-family underdetermination.
+
+The four related results in this packet form one milestone. Repeating them
+for new labels, larger finite meshes or slightly optimized constants would
+not justify another research milestone. Continue personally until the
+authorized deadline while a concrete useful route remains.
